// XFAIL(x86_64-macos): RT-CG-4: x86-64 addresses a frame's slots with 32-bit displacements: a frame of 2 GiB or more cannot be assembled (open)
// XFAIL(x86_64-linux): RT-CG-4: x86-64 addresses a frame's slots with 32-bit displacements: a frame of 2 GiB or more cannot be assembled (open)
// EXPECT: before
// EXIT: 139
// A function with a local of 3 GiB (in a branch not taken): its frame is
// accepted and, being larger than any stack here, its probes fault on the
// guard page as it is entered. On aarch64 it does (exit 139 after
// "before"). On x86-64 the slots past 2 GiB need a displacement that does
// not fit 32 bits. On this branch the x86-64 build refuses it: -O0 with
// "internal error: cannot assemble: an immediate a 64-bit operation cannot
// sign-extend from 32 bits: subq $6442452224, %rsp", -O2 with "a stack
// frame past 2 GB: x86-64 reaches its frame with 32-bit displacements".
// (g302std's 8f4282186 makes every such field an error, never truncated;
// this case comes from its 415738835.) The fix: an offset past 32 bits
// goes through a register (as aarch64's frame addresses do). Run it as
// `tests/run.sh -t x86_64-macos -n rt_cg_004_x86_frame_past_2gib` (at -O0
// and -O 2); on aarch64-macos it passes.
#[inline(never)]
fn big(n: usize) {
    if n > 5 {
        let a = [0u8; 3usize << 30];
        println("{}", a[n]);
    }
    println("inside");
}

fn main() {
    let n = std::env::args().count();
    println("before");
    big(n);
    println("after");
}
